# PLANTED BUG (P-NPM-TOKEN-COMMITTED): an npm registry _authToken committed in .npmrc. The
# npm_ prefix + 36-char body is npm's dedicated automation-token format — a committed one grants
# publish/read access to private packages. Value is FAKE. gitleaks npm-access-token → high.
//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=npm_FAKE0aB1cD2eF3gH4iJ5kL6mN7oP8qR9sT0u

# NEGATIVE (N-NPM-TOKEN-ENV): the same field sourced from an environment variable, the correct
# pattern — no literal token, so gitleaks matches nothing on this line. Cleared.
//registry.example.com/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
